From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp, windows.ui.xaml: composition shapes and animation controllers, element child visuals drawn

Windows.UI.Composition now makes shape visuals and their shapes (container and sprite shapes; path, rectangle, rounded rectangle, ellipse and line geometries; CompositionPath over a program's geometry source; view boxes), gives running animations their AnimationController so a program can pause them and drive their progress, animates booleans, and keeps clip transforms. Windows.UI.Xaml draws the visual a program sets on an element (ElementCompositionPreview) over the element, again when what it draws changes, and gives a program's icon composed over PathIcon its root panel and OnApplyTemplate. Lottie animated visuals draw: Windows Terminal's new-tab dropdown chevron (WinUI 2 AnimatedIcon) was missing.
